<title>INDIA: ANZ Grindlays Bank cuts Indian prime rate.</title>
<headline>ANZ Grindlays Bank cuts Indian prime rate.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>ANZ Grindlays Bank reduced its Indian prime lending rate to 17.0 percent per annum from 17.5 percent with immediate effect, an official at its Bombay office said on Monday.</p>
<p>He said the maximum spread over the prime rate would be 4.0 percent. The cut follows similar reductions by most other banks after the central bank's monetary policy statement on October 19 which boosted liquidity.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
